  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mr Master Samar Ali vs Mr Abdul Salam on 2 August, 2024 -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:30741 Mfa No.5413 of 2013 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 2Nd Day Of August, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice T.G. Shivashankare Gowda Miscellaneous First Appeal No.5413 Of 2013 (Mv-I) Between: Mr. Master Samar Ali S/O. Mohammed Rafiq Minor, Aged About 7 Years Represented By Mother Mrs. Famida Aged About 26 Years R/O. Jamiyabad, Gandhinagar 2Nd Cross, Bhatkal U.K. District. Digitally signed by ...Appellant Prajwal A (By Sri. Nagaraja Hegde, Adv.,) Location: High Court Of And: Karnataka 1. Mr. Abdul Salam S/O Mohammed Ali Kola R/O: Babe Israh,Kargadde Road Nawayath Colony, Bhatkal U.K District. 2. The New India Insurance Company Limited Branch Office, Kundapura Pushpa Building, Main Road Kundapura, Udupi Dist Rep. By Its Branch Manager. ...Respondents (By Sri. K.N. Srinivasa, Adv., For R2 V/O Dtd:06.12.2016 Notice To R1 Is H/S) THIS MFA IS FILED U/S 173(1) OF MV ACT AGAINST THE JUDGMENT AND AWARD DATED:16.03.2013 PASSED IN MVC NO.123/2012 ON THE FILE OF THE SENIOR CIVIL JUDGE, MEMBER, ADDITIONAL MACT, KUNDAPURA, PARTLY ALLOWING THE CLAIM Mr Master Samar Ali vs Mr Abdul Salam on 2 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/187277059/ 1 -2- NC: 2024:KHC:30741 MFA No.5413 of 2013 PETITION FOR COMPENSATION AND SEEKING ENHANCEMENT OF COMPENSATION. THIS APPEAL, COMING ON FOR FINAL HEARING, THIS DAY, JUDGMENT WAS DELIVERED THEREIN AS UNDER: CORAM: HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE T.G. SHIVASHANKARE GOWDA ORAL JUDGMENT",
    "facts": "The petitioner being a minor through his NC: 2024:KHC:30741 guardian mother approached the Tribunal seeking grant of compensation. Claim was opposed by the Insurance Company. After taking the evidence and hearing both parties, the Tribunal by the impugned judgment, assessed compensation of Rs.90,700/-, attributed 50% contributory negligence against the petitioner, and awarded 50% of the compensation i.e., Rs.45,350/- with interest @ 6% per annum. Aggrieved by the same and seeking enhancement of compensation, the petitioner has filed this appeal on various grounds. After alighting from the Auto Rickshaw, he was standing along with his mother on the left side of the road. When the material on record explained that the accident was on the left side of the road, it is not a case of road crossing and thereby the contributory negligence attributing 50% against the Mr Master Samar Ali vs Mr Abdul Salam on 2 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/187277059/ 2",
    "arguments": "The compensation assessed by the tribunal on the meager side is without applying the principle for assessing the compensation in the case of this nature. National Highway is meant for fast moving of the vehicle. It is the duty of the parents to take care of the minor child while crossing the road. The petitioner was crossing the road along with his mother has admitted by the mother herself in the course of cross-examination and for this reason Tribunal has rightly attributed 50% contributory negligence on the part of the petitioner. The petitioner no doubt suffered the injuries, but the compensation assessed is proportionate to the injuries sustained. The medical expenses have been reimbursed by the Tribunal and he has supported the impugned judgment."
  },
